#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:1
msgid "Diagnostics Channel Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:3
msgid "Stability: Experimental."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:5
msgid ""
"Undici supports the "
"[`diagnostics_channel`](https://nodejs.org/api/diagnostics_channel.html) "
"(currently available only on Node.js v16+). It is the preferred way to "
"instrument Undici and retrieve internal information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:8
msgid "The channels available are the following."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:10
msgid "`undici:request:create`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:12
msgid "This message is published when a new outgoing request is created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:28
msgid "Note: a request is only loosely completed to a given socket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:30
msgid "`undici:request:bodyChunkSent`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:32
msgid "This message is published when a chunk of the request body is being sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:42
msgid "`undici:request:bodySent`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:44
msgid "This message is published after the request body has been fully sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:54
msgid "`undici:request:headers`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:56
msgid "This message is published after the response headers have been received."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:70
msgid "`undici:request:bodyChunkReceived`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:72
msgid ""
"This message is published after a chunk of the response body has been "
"received."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:82
msgid "`undici:request:trailers`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:84
msgid ""
"This message is published after the response body and trailers have been "
"received, i.e. the response has been completed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:97
msgid "`undici:request:error`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:99
msgid ""
"This message is published if the request is going to error, but it has "
"not errored yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:109
msgid "`undici:client:sendHeaders`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:111
msgid ""
"This message is published right before the first byte of the request is "
"written to the socket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:113
msgid ""
"*Note*: It will publish the exact headers that will be sent to the server"
" in raw format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:124
msgid "`undici:client:beforeConnect`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:126
msgid ""
"This message is published before creating a new connection for **any** "
"request. You can not assume that this event is related to any specific "
"request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:138
msgid "`undici:client:connected`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:140
msgid "This message is published after a connection is established."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:151
msgid "`undici:client:connectError`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:153
msgid "This message is published if it did not succeed to create new connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:165
msgid "`undici:websocket:open`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:167
msgid ""
"This message is published after the client has successfully connected to "
"a server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:191
msgid "Handshake Response Object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:193
msgid ""
"The `handshakeResponse` object contains the HTTP response that "
"established the WebSocket connection:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:195
msgid ""
"`status` (number): The HTTP status code (`101` for HTTP/1.1 upgrade, "
"`200` for HTTP/2 extended CONNECT)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:196
msgid ""
"`statusText` (string): The HTTP status message (`'Switching Protocols'` "
"for HTTP/1.1, commonly `'OK'` for HTTP/2 in Node.js)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:197
msgid "`headers` (object): The HTTP response headers from the server, including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:198
msgid "`sec-websocket-accept` and other WebSocket-related headers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:199
msgid "`upgrade: 'websocket'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:200
msgid "`connection: 'upgrade'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:202
msgid ""
"The `upgrade` and `connection` headers are only present for HTTP/1.1 "
"handshakes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:204
msgid ""
"This information is particularly useful for debugging and monitoring "
"WebSocket connections, as it provides access to the initial HTTP "
"handshake response that established the WebSocket connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:206
msgid "`undici:websocket:close`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:208
msgid "This message is published after the connection has closed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:220
msgid "`undici:websocket:socket_error`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:222
msgid "This message is published if the socket experiences an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:232
msgid "`undici:websocket:ping`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:234
msgid ""
"This message is published after the client receives a ping frame, if the "
"connection is not closing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:246
msgid "`undici:websocket:pong`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:248
msgid "This message is published after the client receives a pong frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:260
msgid "`undici:proxy:connected`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:262
msgid ""
"This message is published after the `ProxyAgent` establishes a connection"
" to the proxy server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:274
msgid "`undici:request:pending-requests`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:276
msgid ""
"This message is published when the deduplicate interceptor's pending "
"request map changes. This is useful for monitoring and debugging request "
"deduplication behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:278
msgid ""
"The deduplicate interceptor automatically deduplicates concurrent "
"requests for the same resource. When multiple identical requests are made"
" while one is already in-flight, only one request is sent to the origin "
"server, and all waiting handlers receive the same response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:290
msgid "Event Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:292
msgid ""
"`type` (`string`): Either `'added'` when a new pending request is "
"registered, or `'removed'` when a pending request completes (successfully"
" or with an error)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:293
msgid ""
"`size` (`number`): The current number of pending requests after the "
"change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:294
msgid ""
"`key` (`string`): The deduplication key for the request, composed of the "
"origin, method, path, and request headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:296
msgid "Example: Monitoring Request Deduplication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:312
msgid "This can be useful for:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:313
msgid "Verifying that request deduplication is working as expected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:314
msgid "Monitoring the number of concurrent in-flight requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_DiagnosticsChannel.md:315
msgid "Debugging deduplication behavior in production environments"
msgstr ""

